{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And he shall add its fifth.</b> So that he and its fifth equal five (i.e., he adds a fifth of the valuation); and so too for a house, for a field of inheritance, and for second tithe. The reason: when the owner consecrates, he indicates permission for himself and treats the matter lightly, saying, 'Everything is mine — it is enough if I give this much.' Therefore the Torah said that he shall add a fifth to the valuation. But for consecrated movable property, we do not find that the verse required adding a fifth if one comes to redeem it; and since the verse was not particular about their valuation, Shemuel said: consecrated property worth a maneh that one redeemed onto something worth a perutah — is redeemed."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:15:46.817397173Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}